id: pm-beads-1hs9
title: Send acknowledged Beads changes as compact field operations
description: "Generate field operations between two acknowledged Beads snapshots, with explicit removals, source/base digests and a full-snapshot fallback when the base is unavailable. Acceptance: two changed fields among 1,000 records emit exactly two operations plus identity receipts; replay is a no-op; an incorrect base refuses without altering either side. Include typed SDK and CLI, strict bounded validation, property tests, no-git public tracker measurements and npm/Bun CI evidence."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-25T22:00:36.905Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-26T23:31:32.716Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
comments[26]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T22:01:02.491Z",codex-agent,"Overlap recheck: core SDK history and certified complete reads provide revisions and tracker data; Beads reconciliation consumes full snapshots; pending transfer preserves dependency closure; pm-vcs storage and pm-csv import own different boundaries. None supplies acknowledged outbound field operations. Design: a pure, bounded snapshot protocol reuses Beads acknowledgements and existing normalization, emits explicit unset/remove operations and source/base/target receipts, reconstructs a full snapshot before existing reconciliation. No new mutable outbox, lease, checkpoint or tracker mutation path."
  "2026-10-25T22:09:52.930Z",codex-agent,"Implemented stateless typed outbound generation/replay and CLI aliases. Reused the existing acknowledgement digest in persistence and validation. Exact-base inheritance avoids resending unchanged bindings. Targeted protocol suite: 5 tests pass; outgoing module has 100% measured lines, branches and functions. Public read-only no-git copy: 103 records, exactly 2 operations, 1701-byte delta versus 72261-byte full snapshot, unchanged bytes and source tree, replay/no-base fallback verified, wrong-base refused. Seeded SDK state differential and compiled CLI checks are in progress."
  "2026-10-25T22:11:20.966Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: with tests unchanged, reverting only the generateBeadsOutgoingDelta field-change condition to suppress updates makes the 1,000-record acceptance regression fail (expected two field operations, actual zero). Restore passes 5/5; targeted outgoing coverage remains 100% lines/branches/functions. Real compiled CLI passes JSON, TOON, replay and wrong-base checks without git. SDK-configured custom status test passes 32 randomized role registries; transport preserves opaque status values without lifecycle filtering. No mutable shared protocol state exists, so no new lease/journal/retry ownership path is added."
  "2026-10-25T22:15:02.627Z",codex-agent,"Local seeded differential completed: 512 mutation/export/delta/reconciliation sequences pass with native SDK state readbacks, 64 export/upsert round trips, relationships and older revision replay. The final test generator mixes high and low PRNG bits to improve variant coverage; final-head CI reruns that version. Exact-content/new-revision tests also prove replay is revision-bound. Public measurement remains 103 records, 2 operations, 1701 versus 72261 JSON bytes (97.65% smaller), immutable no-git copy. PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-beads/pull/176. CI run 40239127559 already passes fresh-clone strict tracker health on both Node versions; full npm/Bun gates are pending. Local strict health is blocked by a globally installed extension version skew; no dependency pin change or history rewrite is made."
  "2026-10-25T22:16:28.211Z",codex-agent,"The strengthened seeded differential caught a real native round-trip loss in CI at sequence 8: ordinary import joined labels with commas, splitting an SDK-native a,b tag into a and b. Fixed the import boundary by forwarding JSON arrays to the SDK tags parser. Added a short real-SDK export/upsert regression; reverting only that serialization change fails it, restoring passes. The older stub expectation now checks the structured transport value. Initial CI measured 100% across all 15 intended sources but correctly failed this state comparison; no failed gate is claimed as acceptance."
  "2026-10-25T22:18:21.378Z",codex-agent,"Final boundary hardening rejects exotic object prototypes, hidden properties and array subclasses so validated SDK shapes cannot serialize as a different JSON type; null-prototype identity dictionaries remain supported. Protocol tests still pass 5/5 with 100% measured module lines/branches/functions. Tag-boundary regression passes and import-path regressions pass 27/27. Real compiled CLI also verifies a large payload survives host JSON/TOON rendering without truncation. Typecheck, test typecheck, docstring and whitespace checks pass. No remaining local code changes are planned; CI supplies complete npm/Bun gate evidence."
  "2026-10-25T22:25:56.036Z",codex-agent,"Complete CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-beads/actions/runs/40239587335 passed on 19030f6: Node 22 and Node 26, npm and Bun release gates, each 514/514 tests with zero failures/skips/cancellations and 100% measured lines/branches/functions across all 15 intended sources. Fresh-clone strict health and Bun package-graph install pass. A final SDK boundary regression now represents multi-gigabyte shared-string input without materializing it; cumulative payload accounting refuses before whole-value hashing/serialization. Protocol tests still pass 5/5 at 100% module coverage. Final-head CI must repeat the complete gates after this bounded-memory fix; no predecessor run is claimed as final-head evidence."
  "2026-10-26T04:41:59.391Z",codex-agent,"Read-only review blocked producer/consumer agreement and identity ordering. Reusing this item for both classes: define one shared snapshot and acknowledgement schema used by producers and transport validation; preserve live identity/history metadata and legacy receipt bytes through delta and full fallback; replace locale collation with total byte ordering across identity producers/consumers. Add random real-tracker producer-output and Unicode identity properties, separate behavioral revert proofs, and final-head npm/Bun CI evidence. Existing worktree is clean and the prior implementation/evidence is retained."
  "2026-10-26T05:01:41.626Z",codex-agent,"Both blocker classes implemented with one declarative snapshot schema deriving SDK types and validation. Producers canonicalBeadsRecord, parseBeadsSnapshot, readLiveBeadsSnapshot, acknowledgement persistence/read and reconciliation share it; transport uses its record/field/ack descriptors. Live pmId/version/updatedAt metadata and supported schema-1 layouts survive delta/full fallback via metadata/layout receipts. Code-point comparator orders new snapshots, acknowledgements, dependency IDs, transfer selection/topological ties and diff IDs; exact historical ordering is retained as receipt data. Targeted producer/property suite passes 8/8: 512 random Unicode identity sets plus 16 random real non-git trackers spanning all snapshot producers, transfer plan records, previous replay outputs, and legacy on-disk acknowledgements. Existing 512-operation native state differential remains in CI."
  "2026-10-26T05:01:42.786Z",codex-agent,"Separate behavioral revert proofs, tests unchanged: restoring only outgoing.validate to the prior handwritten validator makes the real-tracker producer property fail with invalid_input on live metadata; restoring only compareBeadsIdentities to localeCompare makes the strict Unicode-order property fail on distinct identities that collate equally. Both functions restored. Typecheck and test typecheck pass; docstring lint passes. Final targeted coverage and complete CI release gates will be recorded before handoff."
  "2026-10-26T05:08:23.556Z",codex-agent,"Final targeted coverage passes 8/8 tests with 100% lines/branches/functions for outgoing.ts and snapshot-schema.ts. Linked pm tests pass 5/5 protocol plus 3/3 producer/order checks. Compiled CLI now consumes actual SDK-live acknowledgements containing both canonically equivalent Unicode identities and changed history metadata; JSON, TOON and replay pass. Updated public validation deliberately passes readLiveBeadsSnapshot output directly to acknowledgement, preserving pmId/version/updatedAt: 103 records, exactly 2 operations, 1701-byte delta versus 86596-byte full snapshot, read-only non-git copy and source bytes unchanged. Typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint, changelog check and whitespace check pass. Separate revert proofs are above. Ready for final-head full npm/Bun CI verification."
  "2026-10-26T05:29:43.606Z",codex-agent,"CI run 40272662651 on 3afaaea passed all 517 functional tests on Node 26 but correctly failed unchanged 100% coverage thresholds on two acknowledgement refusal guards. Added one focused real-SDK boundary regression: oversized source refuses without persisting state; a shape-valid tampered SHA or foreign-source receipt refuses without rewriting its file; existing items and valid acknowledgement remain unchanged. Focused reconciliation suite passes 46/46 at 100% lines/branches/functions. Removing only the digest/source integrity guard or only the producer schema guard makes that new test fail with a missing expected rejection; restoring passes. Production code is unchanged from 3afaaea. The obsolete failing run was canceled; new-head full CI must pass before handoff."
  "2026-10-26T22:35:42.023Z",codex-agent,"Re-review found persisted schema-1 transfer ordering drift. Preserve released schema-1 ordering and digests; new plans use schema 2. Add npm-released golden plans, identity journals and acknowledgement fixtures with Unicode identities, resume through the SDK, prove legacy branch necessity, then run targeted checks and CI release gates."
  "2026-10-26T22:41:29.228Z",codex-agent,"Compatibility evidence: npm pack pm-beads@latest resolved 2026.10.26 (tarball SHA-256 17761fded389c1ba91f33223180eb3a44a06ae698c1498d583dfa5c4e5347436). Three frozen fixtures capture released CLI partial transfer, SDK interrupted bootstrap, and live acknowledgement plus reconciliation ledger/checkpoint. All resume retaining original plan digests, core identities and legacy journal formats; SDK-read final fields equal the released result. 512 random Unicode sets validate schema-1 UTF-16 and schema-2 code-point rules independently. Targeted compatibility, transfer and reconciliation: 57/57. Typecheck, test typecheck and docstring lint pass. Behavioral revert proof: removing only schema-1 transfer selection/topology branches fails both released transfer fixtures with invalid_plan (0/2); restoring passes. Removing only legacy reconciliation snapshot collation fails its golden (0/1); restoring gives compatibility 4/4. Old acknowledgement bytes and revisions remain verified unchanged; new reconciliation reservation envelopes explicitly carry schema 2 and digest, historical raw maps remain implicit schema 1 under their owning plan. Full npm and Bun gates will be verified in CI at the pushed head."
  "2026-10-26T22:44:04.171Z",codex-agent,"pm-linked execution passed all three commands: outgoing 5/5, producer agreement 4/4, and compatibility 4/4. Compatibility restores npm-generated UTF-8 artifacts without normalization, runs with no git on PATH, retains schema-1 transfer and reconciliation transaction identifiers and original acknowledgement revisions, and checks both original and resumed identity pins. README records format-version ownership and explicitly forbids implicit migration; fixture provenance includes exact npm integrity and generation program. Compiled outgoing and transfer CLI smoke checks and real SIGKILL checkpoint recovery passed; additional transfer property validation is running before push."
  "2026-10-26T22:45:23.548Z",codex-agent,"Host resource boundary: stopped the additional local integration runner after compiled outgoing CLI, transfer CLI and real SIGKILL recovery had passed. Its remaining 512-row export/upsert pipelines are not counted as local passes and will use the required CI npm/Bun release gate evidence. Required focused compatibility/transfer/reconciliation suite remains 57/57; all 13 pm-linked tests passed. No full release suite was run locally."
  "2026-10-26T22:53:42.030Z",codex-agent,"CI run 40415012844 passed 526/526 tests on both Node versions but correctly failed the unchanged 100 percent branch threshold: reconcile.ts legacy reservation writer branch was not exercised. Add a real SDK regression for a saved schema-1 reconciliation plan before identity bootstrap, proving it allocates and retains the original raw-map format. Existing npm-generated resume fixtures already cover populated legacy journals. No production behavior or threshold changes are needed."
  "2026-10-26T22:54:33.530Z",codex-agent,"Coverage correction verified: compatibility suite 5/5; typecheck, test typecheck and docstring lint pass. New real non-git SDK test saves a schema-1 plan before bootstrap, applies it, and checks the raw reservation map, core identity pins, SDK checkpoint schema/transaction id, final fields and unchanged saved plan bytes. Additional behavioral revert proof: dropping only the schema-1 reservation writer fails this regression (0/1); restoring it passes (1/1). Production code remains byte-identical to the prior pushed compatibility fix. CI 40415012844 was a test-pass/coverage-fail run and is not final release evidence."
  "2026-10-26T22:56:54.285Z",codex-agent,"Final linked verification passed all three commands: outgoing 5/5, producer agreement 4/4, compatibility 5/5 (14 tests, no failures or skips). Typecheck, test typecheck and docstring lint pass. This test-only correction covers the pre-bootstrap schema-1 reservation writer; production sources remain unchanged. The final CI run and exact pushed head will be recorded in the PR body after all npm and Bun release gates pass."
  "2026-10-26T23:04:20.492Z",codex-agent,"CI 40416371748 passed 527/527 tests and 100 percent measured coverage, then failed changelog:check because the pull-request merge context has the published 2026.10.26 base while the branch still has the older package manifest. Align the feature branch with origin/main and regenerate the changelog in that context. Preserve append-only pm history and use any required merge receipt command once; no merge-driver product work. This run is not final full-gate evidence."
  "2026-10-26T23:08:32.835Z",codex-agent,"Aligned the feature branch with origin/main without conflicts. Every origin/main pm history remains an exact byte prefix; no history repair or receipt reconciliation was needed. Adopted only the already-merged upstream dependency pins and refreshed the installation. Compatibility 5/5, typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint and regenerated changelog check pass in this release context. Golden artifact bytes/hashes remain unchanged; generator documentation now pins and verifies its original SDK 2026.10.20 host independently of current development dependencies. Local health retains global extension skew and an inherited advisory provenance vocabulary warning; these are not repaired or concealed. Final npm/Bun release evidence remains pending in CI."
  "2026-10-26T23:18:16.365Z",codex-agent,"Final artifact audit found a pre-existing implicit migration in ownership(): verified legacy document-hash identity pins were rewritten as SDK hash pins during replay. The no-migration requirement applies to these supported older pin receipts too. Retain every non-null verified pin under its original hashKind rules; only a null creation intent may acquire its first SDK hash. Add a real SDK compatibility regression using a restored released schema-1 plan and its existing identities, with a supported legacy document-hash pin. Keep the original plan digest and pin unchanged through completion and replay, and prove the old ownership function fails the regression."
  "2026-10-26T23:22:49.855Z",codex-agent,"No-migration correction passes compatibility plus transfer regressions 17/17 (compatibility 6/6), with typecheck, test typecheck and docstring lint passing. The legacy-pin test restores the published CLI plan, advances only its original checkpoints, changes an owned scratch pin to the supported document-hash format using an SDK document read, then completes a dependent row and replays. The original digest, core identity and exact pin survive. Reverting only ownership() to the previous version fails this test by replacing the old hash and adding hashKind=sdk (0/1); restoring passes. Null creation intents still gain their initial SDK pin normally. Golden files and hashes are unchanged."
  "2026-10-26T23:25:09.444Z",codex-agent,"Linked verification now passes outgoing 5/5, producer agreement 4/4 and compatibility 6/6 (15/15, no failures or skips). Before this final no-migration correction, CI 40417815870 at 937b24e passed all four npm/Bun gates with 527/527 each and 100 percent measured lines, branches and functions for all 16 sources; that validates the aligned release context. The new ownership correction will receive its own final CI release gates after push. Four behavioral revert proofs are recorded: transfer v1 ordering, reconciliation v1 ordering, v1 reservation writer, and immutable legacy hash pins."
  "2026-10-26T23:27:14.110Z",codex-agent,"The immutable-pin early return makes the later !pin.itemHash guard redundant: only null intents reach that block. Remove that unreachable short-circuit alternative before the final coverage gate, keeping the single-entry crash-gap check. Recheck legacy pins and null-intent recovery with focused real-SDK cases; no additional format or migration changes."
  "2026-10-26T23:31:32.713Z",codex-agent,"After simplifying the null-intent guard, focused legacy-pin/crash-gap cases pass 3/3; all four linked commands pass 18 test executions (outgoing 5, producer agreement 4, compatibility 6, focused recovery 3). Typecheck, test typecheck and docstring lint pass. Keep the item claimed/in progress through code validation; record the full 528-test release-gate result before releasing the claim. The final evidence-only commit will also receive clean CI gates. The previous 240010d CI run was superseded by this guard cleanup and canceled rather than counted as release evidence."
